      "side": 1,
      "message": "If it belongs anywhere, the only-update-if-changed logic belongs in charger_set_mode. You\u0027re making the assumption that inhibit mode on the charger is controlled entirely by the EC, and won\u0027t be enabled or disabled by other means than the EC controlling it. I don\u0027t think you can make this assumption for every charger IC. I\u0027m not even sure you can make the assumption for _any_ charger IC -- what if the IC resets for some reason and the registers go back to power-on default?",
      "revId": "73b61225ccb3e7822c4da1eeeb39f0e747901949",
